Disagreements: 3 colleagues back I (misuse-deterrence rationale) but majority note it inverts the actual logic (naloxone increases safety vs. injection). 5 colleagues back V on route-dependency grounds but majority flag internal factual error ("due to the lack of naloxone" in Suboxone). IV rejected by all as evidence base is established, not unknown. 

Errors noted: Q/R duplication in options list; V wording invalidates it for several raters. Current lean: R (II+III) is the only choice with broad, accurate support; no unresolved factual disputes remain.}

